   All considered, IMHO nethack-- adds more variety to nethack (many
new monsters and a few new items), but does not change the game
balance at all.  I never met any of the new unique monsters, and only
one of the new special rooms (the Leprechaun Court).
   

Hilights from Mithrandir's story (with minor spoilers):

   Mithrandir started with a Ro Regeneration (one of the most useful
rings IMHO).  He got an early wish from a fountain: +3 Shield of
Reflection, got +0.  Together with the Cloak of Magic Resistance and
the athame (to engrave E...), that made a good game!  Only my
stupidity could kill him (in a similar situation, I blew a former
incarnation of Mithrandir while a nymph stole my Cloak and I forgot
the loss of magic resistance).
   Mithrandir cleaned out the Mines, got a wish from a lamp in the
Town: blessed PYEC, got a credit card!!! I then discovered that the
Town was a bone level, killed the gost and recoveded the (cursed) PYEC
from a pile.  The candles were gone, though; only two were in the
shop, most annoying.  [Should we tell the DevTeam to forbid special
levels, or at least the Mine Town, from becoming bone levels?  I hate
being short of candles].
   Out of the mines, Mithrandir starts a long sacrificing session,
consuming a spellbook and two wands of create monster; Toth was very
stingy, and gave him only Magicbane and speed.
   Mithrandir gained levels very fast, and he was more then ready for
the Quest when he met the Wizard of Balance.  The Quest was trivial.
   I avoided the cursed Bell abuse (after you make the Quest, the game
is not that difficult anyway).  I also did not genocide, I wanted for
a change to fight Master Liches (the only moster I deem worth
genociding).  I never needed the Ro Conflict.
   Found Medusa level, but no Ring of Levitation or Boots of Water
Walking.  I hate trusting the spell of levitation, so I sent
Mithrandir back to collect rings for polypilling.  By blind luck, on
the next level Mithrandir fell down a trapdoor and landed below
Medusa.
   Cleaning the Castle was easy but tedious (Mithrandir reached level
15 the hard way in the process).  Killed the dragons, got Red DSM (no
fire resistance yet, intrinsic or ring).  Cleaning the Valley also
easy, found Ro Levitation there finally.  
   I got Mithrandir killed by Juiblex by the dumbest move: he was
engulfed by Juiblex while he had his Unicorn Horn inside a blessed Bag
of Holding, and said BoH inside a sack.  "You feel deathly sick".
While fetching the Horn, I hit by mistake M-p [not for the first time
-:(], Moloch is angry...  Mithrandir lost 12 points of protection and
an Amulet of Life Saving -;).
   Everything was easy till the Zoo in the Wizard's Tower, where
Mithrandir needed to cast Charm Monster when surrounded by nasties,
got a pet dragon (Smaug was less useful that I thought).  Zapped a
death ray on the Wizard, got the Book.
   Mithrandir used the first two wishes from the Wand for the missing
5 candles (3 + 2) [no other wishes where needed]; Invocation, down to
the Sanctum.  Hard fighting there, Mithrandir had to cast Fireball and
Charm Monster several times to get elbow room (the hardest part was to
find time for eating, the Ro Regeneration has a price).  The High
Priest was a though one, and Moloch kept zapping Mithrandir.  He
needed to get out of the Shrine twice to recover HPs.
   After that, it was only a matter of keeping the Wizard from
stealing Mithrandir's prized belongings.  I discovered the worth of
the Eye of the Aethiopica (apart from Pw recharging) when the Wizard
managed to steal it: now he was really able to hurt Mithrandir.  A
couple of death rays cured that.
   Mithrandir recovered his treasure (80,000$) left on level 1 (he
could not part from his gold, wizards are so material sometimes... see
my Black Market post), dumped his spellbooks after a last reading, and
proceeded to the Endgame.  Thanks to a Crystal Ball, the Earth, Air,
Water and Fire planes were easy and fast, and the Astral Plane not
difficult either.

